Evaluate rehabilitation through soil, water, ecology, material behavior, and observed outcomes (@mine-rehabilitation-study: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @mining-and-mineral-engineering, #source "../sources/Mine-Rehabilitation-Leading-Practice.lingua#r_4RS2D5ZYYW6Q7EG62C4VDWGWYQ", #source "../sources/Mine-Closure-Leading-Practice.lingua#r_2GYS4C9MHF2CRD8253QPDEV3QN", #source "../sources/Mine-Water-Stewardship-Handbook.lingua#r_4Y8Q03RFJBVBN6WVVY3EN6Q5DM", #mining-and-mineral-engineering "Post-closure-water-ground-monitoring-and-continuing-work.lingua#r_27R2N7NJMBPNJDA0JHMD51F2A9") { r_1TQVJSAJR18YCGPRA48JZXJ6XQ
**Read:** [Mine rehabilitation — Australian leading-practice handbook](../sources/Mine-Rehabilitation-Leading-Practice.lingua#r_4RS2D5ZYYW6Q7EG62C4VDWGWYQ), the complete handbook, including case studies and evaluation methods; [Mine closure — Australian leading-practice handbook](../sources/Mine-Closure-Leading-Practice.lingua#r_2GYS4C9MHF2CRD8253QPDEV3QN), the full relevant completion and long-term performance material; [Water stewardship — Australian leading-practice handbook](../sources/Mine-Water-Stewardship-Handbook.lingua#r_4Y8Q03RFJBVBN6WVVY3EN6Q5DM), the full landform/catchment context used.

Rehabilitation connects constructed ground with soil formation/handling, drainage, erosion, vegetation, organisms, climate, and intended future use. Surface appearance is one observation, not a complete measure of ecological function, ground stability, water quality, or social suitability.

State the baseline, reference conditions, achievable functions, and changes introduced by extraction. Stored soil or growth media have histories of mixing, compaction, moisture, chemistry, and biological change. A successful small plot does not guarantee performance on a whole landform with different slopes, water pathways, material, and weather extremes.

Design observations across space and time, including adverse seasons and disturbed conditions. Compare alternatives with their measured growth, erosion, water, chemistry, maintenance, and use outcomes. Separate rapid establishment from persistent function and distinguish an observed trend from a claim of eventual completion.

**Work:** analyze a complete rehabilitation trial and its later monitoring. Reconstruct the sampling design and material history, compare with an independent/reference area, and evaluate at least one alternative explanation for apparent improvement or failure. Propose a revised field study with explicit observable outcomes and uncertainty. Account for continuing management and how its evidence would change the closure decision. Dedicated agriculture, soil, ecology, and land-use trails deepen the shared living-system knowledge without redefining this mining study.

**Continue:** [Account for the work and knowledge a closed mine can continue to require](Post-closure-water-ground-monitoring-and-continuing-work.lingua#r_27R2N7NJMBPNJDA0JHMD51F2A9).

**Return:** [Mining and mineral engineering — extraction, processing, and continuing work](../Mining-and-mineral-engineering.lingua#r_22HJPS3RTK5EX1J55YJP75PHYA).
